5. earshot — https://github.com/Leonxlnx/earshot
   Copyright (c) 2026 Leon Lin. MIT licence.
   Not built into cav and not redistributed: `cav sfx search --by-sound` asks uv to
   install it (pinned to the v0.3.0 commit) into uv's own cache, and runs it on the
   user's computer. Its models are downloaded from their authors under their own
   licences: CLAP (laion/larger_clap_general) Apache-2.0 and the AudioSet tagger
   (MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593) BSD-3-Clause.
   `cav sfx search --service bank` downloads the earshot source archive (about 4 MB,
   same pinned commit) into the cav cache and renders the sounds its bank describes on
   the user's computer. The synthesized sounds ship under the same MIT licence; the ones
   fitted from a recording credit their CC0 source (author and link) in the manifest.

